# Tool Input Validation

| Field | Value |
| ----- | ----- |
| Issue | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | Draft |

The registry enforces the same JSON Schema it exposes to providers before an executor receives model input.

## Contract

- Missing required input returns a readable ToolResponse naming the required property without invoking the executor; accepted input, including unknown keys, is delivered exactly once without coercion or defaults, and unknown tool names still throw "'`Unknown tool: <name>`.
- Wrong types and enum violations return property paths and failed constraints without executing the tool or exposing input values in returned text or logs.
- Static schemas compile at registration, invalid schemas throw an error naming the tool at registration, and ten subsequent executions reuse the compiled schema without reading it again.
- Function-valued definitions validate against the schema resolved for the current call and cache compilation by resolved schema object identity.

## Integration and delivery

A validation rejection is a tool result for the model'"'s next round; the existing five-round limit bounds retries. The execute method's one-line comment points here for the rejection contract and unknown-name exception. Executor failures retain their existing behavior.

README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md must describe the enforced schema, unmodified extra properties and model-visible rejection. The validator belongs in runtime dependencies. Release delivery requires a MINOR version, an npm-facing changelog entry and the executor migration note from #37.
